.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt KMSHAUNT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kmshaunt
.Nd KMS/DRM console on top of libghostty-vt
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Fl h
.Nm
.Fl V
.Nm
.Fl l
.Op Ar options
.Cm --
.Ar /bin/login
.Op Ar login-arguments
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a system console for Linux.
It drives displays through the Kernel Mode Setting (KMS) and Direct
Rendering Manager (DRM) interfaces, or through fbdev when
.Fl -no-drm
is given, and renders terminal output with libghostty-vt.
One process owns a seat and provides one or more sessions, each with its own
pseudo-terminal and terminal emulator.
.Pp
The command line and configuration file follow
.Xr kmscon 1
version 10.1.0: option names, defaults, grab syntax and parsing rules are
compatible.
Two defaults differ: the
.Ev TERM
value is
.Cm xterm-ghostty ,
and the configuration directory is
.Pa /etc/kmshaunt .
.Pp
.Nm
normally needs root, or a seat obtained through seatd or systemd-logind with
.Fl -libseat ,
to open the virtual terminal and the display devices.
It is usually started on a free virtual terminal by the service manager rather
than from a graphical session.
.Pp
Options may be written as
.Fl -name Ns = Ns Ar value
or
.Fl -name Ar value .
Boolean options take no value and may be negated by prefixing the long name
with
.Cm no- ,
for example
.Fl -no-switchvt .
If an option is given more than once, the last occurrence wins, except
.Fl -mode
and
.Fl -screen ,
which accumulate.
Command-line options are locked: the configuration file cannot override
them.
An unparsable command-line option is ignored with a warning; the same error in
a configuration file aborts loading that file.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss Global Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta"
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Boolean, default off.
Print usage information to standard output and exit.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Boolean, default off.
Print the version; with
.Fl -verbose
also print compile-time information and enabled backends.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Boolean, default off.
Raise the log level to INFO.
.It Fl -debug
Boolean, default off.
Raise the log level to DEBUG; implies
.Fl -verbose .
.It Fl -silent
Boolean, default off.
Only log warnings and errors.
.It Fl c Ar dir , Fl -configdir Ar dir
String, default
.Pa /etc/kmshaunt .
Use
.Ar dir
as the configuration directory containing
.Pa kmshaunt.conf
and the per-seat
.Pa <seat>.seat.conf
files.
.El
.Ss Seat Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta"
.It Fl -vt Ar vt
Virtual terminal specification (string), default auto-detect.
A number
.Ar N
selects
.Pa /dev/ttyN ;
a value beginning with a period or a slash is used verbatim as the device
path;
every other value is prefixed with
.Pa /dev/ ,
so
.Cm tty2
also selects
.Pa /dev/tty2 .
When unset, the controlling terminal is used if it is a VT, otherwise a free
VT is allocated.
.It Fl -switchvt
Boolean, default on.
Activate the VT at startup and restore the previously active VT on exit.
.It Fl -libseat
Boolean, default off.
Acquire the seat and its devices through libseat (seatd or systemd-logind)
instead of opening the VT and DRM devices directly.
.El
.Ss Session Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta"
.It Fl -session-max Ar num
Unsigned integer, default 50.
Maximum number of sessions; 0 means no limit.
.It Fl -session-control
Boolean, default off.
Enable the session grabs that create, cycle and close sessions.
It is disabled automatically on real virtual terminals.
.El
.Ss Terminal Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta"
.It Fl -issue
Boolean, default on.
Write the issue text collected from
.Fl -issue-path
to each new session before the login process starts.
.It Fl -issue-path Ar path
String, default
.Cm /etc/issue ,
.Cm /etc/issue.d ,
.Cm /run/issue ,
.Cm /run/issue.d ,
.Cm /usr/lib/issue
and
.Cm /usr/lib/issue.d ,
colon-separated.
Files are read in order, directories are scanned for
.Pa *.issue
files in lexicographic order, and the total is capped at 256 KiB.
.It Fl -asciicast Ar file
String, unset by default.
Play the asciicast v2 or v3 recording
.Ar file
into a new session.
Playback stops on the first key press.
.It Fl -asciicast-loop
Boolean, default off.
Restart asciicast playback when the recording ends.
.It Fl l , Fl -login Ar argv
Login argv (argument list); the default is
.Cm /bin/login -p
(or
.Cm /bin/login
with
.Fl -no-reset-env ) .
On the command line, everything after the first
.Cm --
argument becomes the login argv.
In a configuration file the value is split into argv with shell-like quoting.
.It Fl -oneshot
Boolean, default off.
Close the session when the login process exits, and exit
.Nm
if it was the last session.
Intended for setup scripts and prompts such as disk-encryption unlock.
.It Fl t Ar TERM , Fl -term Ar TERM
String, default
.Cm xterm-ghostty .
Set
.Ev TERM
to
.Ar TERM
in every session.
.It Fl -reset-env
Boolean, default on.
Start children with an empty environment, then set only
.Ev TERM ,
.Ev COLORTERM ,
.Ev XDG_SEAT ,
.Ev XDG_VTNR ,
.Ev TERM_SESSION_TYPE
and
.Ev KMS_START_SCRIPT .
When disabled, the parent environment is inherited and the default login argv
is
.Cm /bin/login
without the
.Fl p
argument.
.It Fl -backspace-delete
Boolean, default on.
Make the Backspace key send DEL (0x7f) to applications.
.It Fl -sb-size Ar num
Unsigned integer, default 1000.
Scrollback buffer size in lines; 0 disables scrollback.
.It Fl -bell
Boolean, default off.
Forward the terminal bell from applications to the virtual terminal.
.It Fl -blink
Boolean, default on.
Enable cursor and text blinking.
.El
.Ss Input Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta"
.It Fl -xkb-model Ar model
String, unset by default (uses the XKB default).
XKB keyboard model.
.It Fl -xkb-layout Ar layout
String, unset by default.
XKB layout, for example
.Cm de .
.It Fl -xkb-variant Ar variant
String, unset by default.
XKB layout variant.
.It Fl -xkb-options Ar options
String, unset by default.
Comma-separated XKB options.
.It Fl -xkb-keymap Ar file
String, unset by default.
Load the precompiled keymap
.Ar file .
It takes precedence over the model, layout, variant and options settings; an
empty value disables the keymap file.
.It Fl -xkb-compose-file Ar file
String, unset by default.
Use
.Ar file
as the compose file.
When unset or empty, the default compose file for the current locale is used.
.It Fl -xkb-repeat-delay Ar msecs
Unsigned integer, default 250.
Delay in milliseconds before key repeat starts.
.It Fl -xkb-repeat-rate Ar msecs
Unsigned integer, default 50.
Interval in milliseconds between repeated keys.
.It Fl -mouse
Boolean, default on.
Capture the pointer, enable text selection with copy and paste, and scroll the
scrollback with the wheel.
.It Fl -natural-scrolling
Boolean, default off.
Invert the wheel direction.
.It Fl -soft-cursor
Boolean, default off.
Always draw a software cursor instead of a hardware cursor plane.
.It Fl -dpms-timeout Ar secs
Unsigned integer, default 600.
Blank the display after
.Ar secs
seconds without input; 0 disables the timeout.
Any input unblanks the display and restarts the timer.
.El
.Ss Grabs
Each grab option takes a grab specification and is disabled when the value is
empty.
The syntax is described in
.Xr kmshaunt.conf 5 ;
an event matches only when its modifier set is exactly the configured set.
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta"
.It Fl -grab-scroll-up Ar grab
Grab, default
.Cm <Shift>Up .
Scroll the scrollback back one line.
.It Fl -grab-scroll-down Ar grab
Grab, default
.Cm <Shift>Down .
Scroll the scrollback forward one line.
.It Fl -grab-page-up Ar grab
Grab, default
.Cm <Shift>Prior .
Scroll the scrollback back one page.
.It Fl -grab-page-down Ar grab
Grab, default
.Cm <Shift>Next .
Scroll the scrollback forward one page.
.It Fl -grab-zoom-in Ar grab
Grab, default
.Cm <Ctrl>plus
or
.Cm <Ctrl>equal .
Increase the font size.
.It Fl -grab-zoom-out Ar grab
Grab, default
.Cm <Ctrl>minus .
Decrease the font size.
.It Fl -grab-session-next Ar grab
Grab, default
.Cm <Ctrl><Logo>Right .
Switch to the next session; requires
.Fl -session-control .
.It Fl -grab-session-prev Ar grab
Grab, default
.Cm <Ctrl><Logo>Left .
Switch to the previous session; requires
.Fl -session-control .
.It Fl -grab-session-close Ar grab
Grab, default
.Cm <Ctrl><Logo>BackSpace .
Close the current session; requires
.Fl -session-control .
.It Fl -grab-terminal-new Ar grab
Grab, default
.Cm <Ctrl><Logo>Return .
Create a new session; requires
.Fl -session-control .
.It Fl -grab-rotate-cw Ar grab
Grab, default
.Cm <Logo>plus
or
.Cm <Logo>equal .
Rotate all displays clockwise.
.It Fl -grab-rotate-ccw Ar grab
Grab, default
.Cm <Logo>minus .
Rotate all displays counter-clockwise.
.It Fl -grab-reboot Ar grab
Grab, disabled by default.
Reboot the system.
A soft or hard reboot is chosen according to
.Pa /proc/sys/kernel/ctrl-alt-del .
.El
.Ss Video Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta"
.It Fl -drm
Boolean, default on.
Use DRM devices and ignore fbdev devices.
When disabled, only fbdev devices are used.
.It Fl -hwaccel
Boolean, default off.
Use the DRM 3D (OpenGL ES) backend.
If it cannot be initialized,
.Nm
falls back to the DRM 2D backend.
.It Fl -gpus Ar list
GPU selection (enumeration), default
.Cm all .
One of
.Cm all ,
.Cm aux
(primary and auxiliary GPUs) or
.Cm primary .
.Cm auxiliary
and
.Cm single
are accepted as aliases for
.Cm aux
and
.Cm primary .
.It Fl -use-original-mode
Boolean, default off.
Do not change the display mode; keep the mode already set by the firmware or a
previous owner.
This option cannot be combined with
.Fl -mode :
if both are given,
.Fl -use-original-mode
is cleared with a warning.
.It Fl -mode Ar spec
Mode list, empty by default, repeatable.
Set the mode for matching displays.
The form is
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[gpu][connector]WIDTHxHEIGHT[@RATE]
.Ed
for example
.Cm card0[HDMI-A-1]1920x1080@60
or
.Cm 1920x1080@60 .
Only the DRM backends use modes; the first match wins, in the order
GPU and connector, connector only, then global entries.
.It Fl -multi-monitor Ar policy
String, default
.Cm scaled .
Combine multiple monitors with
.Cm largest
(only the largest monitor is used),
.Cm scaled
(the smallest monitor sets the text grid and larger monitors scale the font),
or
.Cm clone
(all monitors show the same size).
Any other value behaves like
.Cm clone .
.It Fl -screen Ar spec
Screen list, empty by default, repeatable.
Set the orientation of matching displays, or disable them.
The form is
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[gpu][connector]normal|left|right|upside-down|disabled
.Ed
for example
.Cm card0[DP-1]right ,
.Cm [HDMI-A-1]left
or
.Cm disabled .
Matching uses the same precedence as
.Fl -mode .
A disabled display is not used unless it is the only available display.
.El
.Ss Font Options
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta"
.It Fl -font-engine Ar engine
String, unset by default.
Select a font backend by name:
.Cm freetype ,
.Cm pango ,
.Cm unifont ,
.Cm psf
or
.Cm 8x16 .
When unset or unavailable, the first working backend of the chain
freetype, pango, unifont, psf, 8x16 is used.
.It Fl -font-size Ar pixels
Unsigned integer, default 0.
Font size in pixels; 0 selects a size from the physical display size.
.It Fl -font-name Ar name
String, default
.Cm monospace .
Fontconfig family or pattern for the freetype and pango backends, or a font
file path for the psf backend.
.El
.Ss Palette Options
Colors are specified as
.Ar r , Ns Ar g , Ns Ar b
with components from 0 to 255.
They are used only when
.Fl -palette
is set to
.Cm custom .
.Bl -tag -width "-palette-light-magenta"
.It Fl -palette Ar name
String, unset by default (legacy palette).
Select a palette preset:
.Cm custom ,
.Cm nord ,
.Cm solarized ,
.Cm solarized-black ,
.Cm solarized-white ,
.Cm soft-black ,
.Cm base16-dark ,
.Cm base16-light ,
.Cm vga
or
.Cm legacy .
Unknown names select the legacy palette.
.It Fl -palette-black Ar r,g,b
Color, default 0,0,0.
ANSI color 0 (black).
.It Fl -palette-red Ar r,g,b
Color, default 205,0,0.
ANSI color 1 (red).
.It Fl -palette-green Ar r,g,b
Color, default 0,205,0.
ANSI color 2 (green).
.It Fl -palette-yellow Ar r,g,b
Color, default 205,205,0.
ANSI color 3 (yellow).
.It Fl -palette-blue Ar r,g,b
Color, default 0,0,238.
ANSI color 4 (blue).
.It Fl -palette-magenta Ar r,g,b
Color, default 205,0,205.
ANSI color 5 (magenta).
.It Fl -palette-cyan Ar r,g,b
Color, default 0,205,205.
ANSI color 6 (cyan).
.It Fl -palette-light-grey Ar r,g,b
Color, default 229,229,229.
ANSI color 7 (light grey).
.It Fl -palette-dark-grey Ar r,g,b
Color, default 127,127,127.
ANSI color 8 (dark grey).
.It Fl -palette-light-red Ar r,g,b
Color, default 255,0,0.
ANSI color 9 (light red).
.It Fl -palette-light-green Ar r,g,b
Color, default 0,255,0.
ANSI color 10 (light green).
.It Fl -palette-light-yellow Ar r,g,b
Color, default 255,255,0.
ANSI color 11 (light yellow).
.It Fl -palette-light-blue Ar r,g,b
Color, default 92,92,255.
ANSI color 12 (light blue).
.It Fl -palette-light-magenta Ar r,g,b
Color, default 255,0,255.
ANSI color 13 (light magenta).
.It Fl -palette-light-cyan Ar r,g,b
Color, default 0,255,255.
ANSI color 14 (light cyan).
.It Fl -palette-white Ar r,g,b
Color, default 255,255,255.
ANSI color 15 (white).
.It Fl -palette-foreground Ar r,g,b
Color, default 229,229,229.
Default foreground color.
.It Fl -palette-background Ar r,g,b
Color, default 0,0,0.
Default background color.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev TERM
Set in every session to the value of
.Fl -term
(default
.Cm xterm-ghostty ) .
.It Ev COLORTERM
Set to
.Cm truecolor .
.It Ev XDG_SEAT
Name of the seat that owns the session.
.It Ev XDG_VTNR
Number of the virtual terminal used by the seat.
.It Ev TERM_SESSION_TYPE
Set to
.Cm kms
on DRM seats and to
.Cm fb
on fbdev seats.
.It Ev KMS_START_SCRIPT
Name of the
.Cm kmshaunt-launch-gui
helper, which releases DRM master and then runs a graphical program; set on
DRM seats only.
.It Ev LC_ALL , Ev LC_CTYPE , Ev LANG
Select the locale used to find the default compose file when
.Fl -xkb-compose-file
is unset.
.Cm C
is used when none of them is set.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kmshaunt/kmshaunt.conf
Main configuration file.
Its location follows
.Fl -configdir .
.It Pa /etc/kmshaunt/<seat>.seat.conf
Per-seat configuration file, normally
.Pa /etc/kmshaunt/seat0.seat.conf .
It is layered over the main file and cannot override command-line options.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start
.Nm
on the first free virtual terminal with the default settings:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kmshaunt
.Ed
.Pp
Run a one-shot command on virtual terminal 3 and exit when it finishes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kmshaunt --vt=3 --oneshot -l -- /bin/sh -c 'echo hello'
.Ed
.Pp
Use a custom font and a larger scrollback:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kmshaunt --font-name='Source Code Pro' --font-size=16 --sb-size=10000
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kmscon 1 ,
.Xr kmshaunt.conf 5